  "summary": "An ordered composition in which an agent acquires a held object, relocates to a destination, opens a container at that destination, cools the held object at that station, and finally delivers the object to a target location. One concrete object identity is carried from acquisition through cooling and delivery, and one concrete location identity is shared between the relocation, the container opening, and the cooling station. Ordering is expressed entirely by the fixed occurrence sequence, so the composition keeps only identity-preserving flows and reuses the already-active object flow; the externally supplied final destination has no in-sequence producer and is left unlinked.",
